### 7. Is there independent corroboration from at least two reputable news sources reporting on the Iowa Farm Bureau's decision not to endorse Joni Ernst in 2020?
Answer: Based on the search result, the Iowa Farm Bureau explicitly denied this claim, stating that a fake email had been circulating about Senator Ernst no longer having their support, and that "any news reports that speak to its validity are false." The Iowa Farm Bureau actually "proudly designated her as a Friend of Agriculture," directly contradicting the claim. Therefore, there is no independent corroboration from reputable news sources because the underlying claim itself was debunked by the Iowa Farm Bureau.

Source URL: https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/Statement-by-Iowa-Farm-Bureau-Federation

### 9. Did the Iowa Farm Bureau endorse any other candidates in the same 2020 election cycle, and if so, who?
Answer: Yes, according to the search result, the Iowa Farm Bureau's political arm also endorsed Republican Randy Feenstra in the same 2020 election cycle. As stated in the article, "The Iowa Farm Bureau's political arm endorsed Republicans Joni Ernst and Randy Feenstra in their respective election races." Feenstra was running in western Iowa's 4th Congressional District against Democrat J.D. Scholten, after having defeated longtime Republican incumbent U.S. Rep. Steve King in the GOP primary.

