### Justification
The claim is false. The Iowa Farm Bureau's Political Action Committee (PAC) actually **endorsed** Sen. Joni Ernst for her 2020 re-election, designating her a "Friend of Agriculture" in September 2020, as confirmed by the [Iowa Farm Bureau's own article](https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/FB-designates-Friends-of-Ag) and reported by the [Quad City Times](https://qctimes.com/news/state-and-regional/govt-and-politics/campaign-almanac-for-wednesday-september-9-2020/article_78f6dbc5-6272-547c-9de9-e2a78cefb8cf.html) and [Caffeinated Thoughts](https://caffeinatedthoughts.com/2020/09/iowa-farm-bureau-pac-endorses-ernst-feenstra-and-young/). The Iowa Farm Bureau also issued an explicit [statement](https://www.iowafarmbureau.com/Article/Statement-by-Iowa-Farm-Bureau-Federation) debunking the rumor, noting that a "fake email" was circulating and that "any news reports that speak to its validity are false," while reaffirming it "proudly designated her as a Friend of Agriculture." Multiple independent sources uniformly confirm the endorsement rather than any withdrawal, making the claim unambiguously refuted.